    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0095" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 287.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 1, 1863,</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Learning from the consul at Liverpool that
                    the person reported as the purchaser of the Sumter is a man well known in that
                    place as the agent of Messrs. Fraser, Trenholm &amp; Co., I immediately
                    addressed a note to Lord Russell on the subject, a copy of which I have the
                    honor to transmit.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d23-a1.xml" xpointer="d23-a1"/>
            </div>
